  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Grant Aid for Humanitarian Assistance in the Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The heavy clashes between the Rapid Support Forces and the Sudanese Armed Forces that erupted on 15 April 2023, mainly in Khartoum and the Darfur region but also in other states of Sudan, has severely affected millions. Prior to the unfolding crisis, approximately one-third of the population in Sudan was already receiving humanitarian assistance. As of the beginning of May 2023, more than 900 people have been killed, over 5,000 injured and almost two million displaced. With numbers continuing to increase, this has resulted in a devasting humanitarian situation in and around countries bordering Sudan and the region, creating an additional need in a situation that was already in crisis. 
 
In response to the unfolding crisis, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) is conducting a six-month project that provides humanitarian assistance to the most vulnerable internally displaced persons in Sudan. The project activities include the procurement of full non-food item kits; identification of target areas based on latest displacement information and critical needs identified amongst internally displaced persons from IOM&apos;s Displacement Tracking Matrix; conducting assessments in the targeted areas; distribution of full non-food item kits in targeted areas; and conducting post-distribution monitoring missions.</narrative>
  </description>
